Task 2: Link the Project to a Git Repository
Subtask 2.1: Prepare a Sample Git Repository
For this lab, we'll use a public repository with sample Ansible content. If you want to create your own repository, follow these steps:

Create a simple directory structure on your local system or use the provided sample repository:
mkdir ansible-lab-project
cd ansible-lab-project

# Create a simple playbook
cat > site.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Simple web server setup
  hosts: web
  become: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Install Apache
      package:
        name: httpd
        state: present
    
    - name: Start Apache service
      service:
        name: httpd
        state: started
        enabled: yes
EOF

# Create an inventory file
cat > inventory << 'EOF'
[web]
webserver1 ansible_host=192.168.1.10
webserver2 ansible_host=192.168.1.11
EOF

# Create a simple role structure
mkdir -p roles/webserver/tasks
cat > roles/webserver/tasks/main.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Install web server packages
  package:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop:
    - httpd
    - mod_ssl
EOF
