Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Sync Fails with Authentication Error
Problem: Git repository requires authentication but no credentials provided

Solution:

# Create credential in Automation Controller
1. Go to Credentials → Add
2. Select "Source Control" credential type
3. Provide username/password or SSH key
4. Link credential to project
Issue 2: Sync Fails with Network Connectivity
Problem: Cannot reach Git repository URL

Solution:

# Test connectivity from controller host
curl -I https://github.com/ansible/ansible-examples.git
# Check firewall and proxy settings
Issue 3: No Playbooks Detected After Sync
Problem: Project syncs successfully but no playbooks appear

Solution:

Verify repository contains .yml or .yaml files in root directory
Check that files follow Ansible playbook format
Ensure files are not in subdirectories (unless specified)
Issue 4: Sync Hangs or Times Out
Problem: Synchronization process doesn't complete

Solution:

# Check repository size and network speed
# Consider using shallow clone for large repositories
# Verify no proxy or firewall blocking
