Best Practices
Project Organization
• Use descriptive project names that reflect their purpose • Organize repositories with clear directory structures • Include README files with project documentation • Use version tags for stable releases

Security Considerations
• Use private repositories for sensitive automation content • Implement proper access controls on Git repositories • Regularly rotate credentials used for repository access • Audit project access and synchronization logs

Performance Optimization
• Use shallow clones for large repositories • Configure appropriate cache timeouts based on change frequency • Monitor sync job performance and optimize as needed • Clean up old project revisions periodically

